  "teaId": "magdalene-first",
  "text": "Everybody went home. She stayed and cried in a graveyard. So she's the one who saw him first.\n\nJohn twenty. Mary Magdalene comes to the tomb while it's still dark, sees the stone gone, and runs for Peter and John. They sprint back, look in, see the linen, and then the text says it plainly. They went away again unto their own home.\n\nThey left.\n\nShe didn't. Mary stood without at the sepulchre weeping.\n\nSo she's the one there when two angels ask why she's crying. And she says, \"Because they have taken away my Lord, and I know not where they have laid him.\"\n\nThen she turns around, sees a man, and thinks he's the gardener. Says, \"Sir, if thou have borne him hence, tell me where thou hast laid him, and I will take him away.\"\n\nShe's devastated and still trying to handle the logistics herself.\n\nAnd he says one word. \"Mary.\"\n\nThat's it. That's the whole thing. He says her name and she knows.\n\nThen he sends her. Go to my brethren and tell them.\n\nAnd Mary Magdalene came and told the disciples that she had seen the Lord.\n\nThe resurrection gets announced by a woman who wouldn't leave.",
